{
 "page": "29-landlords.html",
 "_": "Footage windows on 29-landlords (defaults, no at= overrides). THE CAMERA MOVES, so each window moves with it: rect / rect_4k are the window at its first visible frame, and track_4k is the footage area for EVERY visible frame, in order from visible_open.in_f to visible_open.out_f \u00e2\u02c6\u2019 1 ([x, y, w, h] in 4K px, already rounded; footage frame k goes at track_4k[k], resized to w \u00c3\u2014 h; the aspect stays 16:9). The crane is screen-fixed (moves: false). Rects are the FOOTAGE AREA; the page draws a 2 px cream frame just OUTSIDE each one (4 px at 4K), so footage pasted exactly into the rect sits inside it. Times are seconds from the page's first frame (page 0 = VO 353.96); frames at 30 fps. Render the edit's copy with slots=0 (every window a flat #050507 ground). The four gold windows are lit together and shut together at the same frame; so are the two amber ones. A window that is open longer than its footage holds the footage's last frame (at most 6 frames: Microsoft). Generated by the page itself (29-landlords.html?slotsjson).",
 "fps": 30,
 "page_start_vo": 353.96,
 "page_seconds": 21.3,
 "wipe": "Opening: eased (cubic in-out) over 'opening' (0.28 s): the window first grows as a 2 px horizontal line from its centre out to full width, then opens vertically from its centre line to full height. Closing is the reverse over 'closing' (0.22 s). Simplest composite: paste footage from visible_open.in_f to visible_open.out_f \u00e2\u02c6\u2019 1 at track_4k (the window shows its dark ground during the wipes).",
 "composite": "for k, (x, y, w, h) in enumerate(slot.track_4k): frame = visible_open.in_f + k; paste footage[min(k, len \u00e2\u02c6\u2019 1)] resized to (w, h) at (x, y). The n > len + 6 guard in render-38.py holds here.",
